+/**
+ * How much of a job is in our bindings at all (VitaSurf).
+ *
+ * childNodes was the suspect and it is not: 36,047 rebuilds produced
+ * 38,539 children, a list of one on average, for 300 ms. Everything
+ * counted so far comes to about 3.3 s of a job that runs 12,090, so
+ * either the rest is in bindings nobody counts or it is the
+ * interpreter itself, and those want opposite fixes.
+ *
+ * Nearly every node binding starts by turning its JSValue back into a
+ * dom_node, so counting that one place bounds the question without
+ * touching two hundred functions. textContent and cloneNode are
+ * counted apart because both walk a subtree, which is the shape that
+ * would hide seconds.
+ */
